  "result": "`click.KeyValue` is implemented and the full test suite passes. I haven't committed anything.\n\n- **`src/click/types.py`**: new `KeyValue(ParamType)` class. It splits on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`, and an empty value such as `a=` is allowed. A missing `=` or an empty key fails with `'\u2026' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n- **`src/click/__init__.py`**: exports `KeyValue`.\n- **`CHANGES.md`**: 8.5.0 was already released on 2026-08-24, so I added a new \"Version 8.6.0 / Unreleased\" section with the entry. The `versionadded` directive also says 8.6.0. Adjust both if the next release has a different number.\n- **Docs**: entries in `docs/api.md` and `docs/parameter-types.md`.\n- **`tests/test_types.py`**: direct `convert()` success and failure cases, plus a `CliRunner` test that checks `--set a=1 --set b=2=3` and the error exit code (2) for `--set novalue`.\n\n`pytest` gives 1914 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed, and `ruff check` is clean. I couldn't run mypy because it isn't installed in this environment.\n\nI first put the new tests between `test_range`'s decorator and its function, which would have broken that test. I moved them above it and reran the suite.",
